<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: SOCCER-CZECH REPUBLIC BEAT MALTA 6-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-CZECH REPUBLIC BEAT MALTA 6-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>TEPLICE, Czech Republic 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Republic beat Malta 6-0 (halftime 2-0) in a World Cup European group six soccer qualifier on on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorers - Patrik Berger (12th minute, 62nd penalty), Pavel Nedved (24th), Lubos Kubik (77th), Vladimir Smicer (83rd), Martin Frydek (87th)</p>
<p>Attendence: 11,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under - played, won, drawn, lost, goals for, against, points):</p>
<p> Yugoslavia	     2   2   0   0   9   1   6</p>
<p> Czech Republic	 1   1   0   0   6   0   3</p>
<p> Spain		    1   1   0   0   6   2   3</p>
<p> Slovakia		 1   1   0   0   2   1   3</p>
<p> Faroe Islands	  3   0   0   3   4  11   0</p>
<p> Malta		    2   0   0   2   0  12   0</p>
<p>Next match: Sept 22 - Slovakia v Malta</p>
</text>
